        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): bound MiniMax VLM JSON response reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`minimaxUnderstandImage` in `src/agents/minimax-vlm.ts` uses unbounded `res.json()` to parse the MiniMax VLM API response. A large or malicious response body would be fully buffered into memory before parsing, creating an OOM vector.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace `res.json()` with the existing `readProviderJsonResponse()` helper (from `src/agents/provider-http-errors.ts`), which wraps `readResponseWithLimit()` with a 16 MiB default cap. This matches the pattern used by other provider response readers in the codebase and the recent OOM-hardening PRs (#99014, #98844, #98480, #96347).\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents potential out-of-memory crashes when the MiniMax VLM API returns unexpectedly large responses.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real behavior proof — `readProviderJsonResponse` contract:**\n```\nInput:   Response with 17 MiB body (> 16 MiB cap)\nResult:  rejects with \"minimax VLM: JSON response exceeds 16777216 bytes\"\n\nInput:   Response with valid small JSON body\nResult:  parses and returns the JSON object correctly\n```\n\n**Unit tests added (4 tests):**\n- `isMinimaxVlmProvider` recognizes minimax variants\n- `isMinimaxVlmProvider` rejects non-minimax providers\n- `readProviderJsonResponse` rejects oversized response bodies before parsing\n- `readProviderJsonResponse` parses valid bounded JSON responses\n\n**Validation:**\n- `pnpm test src/agents/minimax-vlm.test.ts`: **4 tests passed**\n- tsgo typecheck: passed\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
